  "title": {
    "rendered": "Orford Landing Page"
  },
  "content": {
    "rendered": "\n<h1>\n\t\t\tOrford, Your Fiber Network Is Here!\t</h1>\n\t<p>LymeFiber is pleased to announce that fiber optic internet is now available in select areas of Orford. Our basic service delivers <strong>100 Mbps symmetrical speeds for $72 per month</strong>. Optional telephone service, which can replace your Consolidated or Topsham bill, is available for <strong>$25 per month</strong>. Higher speed plans are also offered, including options up to <strong>1 Gigabit per second</strong>.</p>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://order.lymefiber.net\" target=\"_self\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSign Up Now!\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n<h2>\n\t\t\tWhy Households in Orford Choose LymeFiber\t</h2>\n\t<ul>\n<li>Symmetrical upload and download speeds</li>\n<li>No data caps or throttling</li>\n<li>Locally built and operated</li>\n<li>Reliable service during peak hours and storms</li>\n<li>Optional telephone service for $25 per month</li>\n</ul>\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://order.lymefiber.net\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCheck My Address\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t<blockquote>\n<p><strong>LymeFiber Service available north from the Lyme/Orford Town Border</strong></p>\n<p>River Rd. North to Rt. 10 intersection, including Sanborn Lane</p>\n<p>Route 10 north to 712 Dartmouth College Hwy (Rt. 10)</p>\n<p>Including the following roads connecting to Rt.10:</p>\n<p>Tree Farm Road to EOL</p>\n<p>Sawyer Brook Road to EOL</p>\n<p>Boat Landing Road Pole line on the road</p>\n<p>Hebb Drive to EOL</p>\n<p>Rte. 25A east from Rt. 10 to 2959 Rt. 25A</p>\n<p>Rte. 25A (Bridge St.) west from Rt. 10 to the Connecticut River</p>\n<p>Archertown Rd., east to the intersection with Tannery Rd., and Tannery Rd</p>\n<p>709 &amp; 712 route 10 Bellmore Dr</p>\n</blockquote>\n\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" src=\"\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\t<p>LymeFiber was created to bring <strong>reliable high-speed internet</strong> to communities that have been underserved for years. Our network is designed to support work-from-home, online learning, telehealth, and modern home technology.</p>\n<p>We take pride in <strong>serving our neighbors with responsive, local support.</strong></p>\n\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" src=\"\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" onerror=\"this.style.display='none'\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n",
    "protected": false
  },
